um", "notes": ["Open seat: Elise Stefanik (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "NY-21 is an open seat after Elise Stefanik's retirement, and both parties have invested heavily: Constantino has raised about $9.5 million and Gendebien about $5.5 million, leaving both well-funded. The district's R+10 baseline favors Republicans, and most expert raters call the race Likely R, though The Economist rates it Lean R and Democrats have added it to their Red to Blue program.\n\nPolling has been volatile. Surveys in August and September split between the candidates, but the most recent and highest-quality poll, a Times Union/Siena survey of likely voters in early October, shows Gendebien ahead 46-42. Prediction markets still price the Republican near 70 percent. The race looks competitive but leans Republican on the district's fundamentals, with genuine uncertainty about which signal holds.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1406, "margin": -6.22}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2036, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1958, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2007, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1538, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1549, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2301, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2417, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1919, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1959, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1935, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1967, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2046, "margin": -5.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.1363, "margin": -6.8}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.1525, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.1259, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.1676, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.3186, "margin": -2.5}]}